I'm sure it works sometimes, but I've lost too many healers to him to
count on it! The problem being that there're too many other things that
could wake him up before you can get into firing range.  In this
particular case, I didn't have waterwalking or levitaition, so was
relying on freezing water to cross it - if I'd stumbled on the ice,
that would have woken him up, and I'd have been miles from the up
stairs.

Generally I just camp on the up stairs, deal with all the eels first,
while waiting for him to wake up - he teleports in, generally gets two
hits - goodbye two levels (I'm generally fast, but not very fast at
this point), zap him with the wand, pray it doesn't miss!, then as you
say, keep alternating hitting him and zapping him.  I generally find
that even doing that he'll wake up at least once before I can put him
back to sleep again.

Maybe I'm just being hasty, and should guarantee that I have lev. or WW
before doing the quest - but I really like the staff, (plus all the
dragons for their scale drops!), and generally do it before Medusa etc.

